WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:02.968
-Welcome back, everybody.
We're here with Gayle King!

00:00:02.968 --> 00:00:05.105
Costume change!

00:00:05.105 --> 00:00:07.340
-First time ever.
-First-time costume change.

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:09.376
-First time ever.
-It might become a thing now.

00:00:09.376 --> 00:00:10.543
-Yeah.

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:11.678
-It's addicting once you do
a costume change.

00:00:11.678 --> 00:00:12.879
Alright, let's get started.

00:00:12.879 --> 00:00:16.015
This looks like a real thing
here right now.

00:00:16.015 --> 00:00:17.917
-Yeah. So --
-This was -- This just went on.

00:00:17.917 --> 00:00:19.786
-Yeah, so it's a warmer.
-It's a warmer.

00:00:19.786 --> 00:00:23.956
-So, there's 104 items.
Price range from $18 to $900.

00:00:23.956 --> 00:00:26.092
The most expensive
is an espresso.

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:28.761
But this, we thought,
was very cool because this is --

00:00:28.761 --> 00:00:31.630
You could call this the Uber
or the iPhone of toasters.

00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:33.299
-Okay.
-You can get six

00:00:33.299 --> 00:00:36.136
different shades of brownness
depending on what you like.

00:00:36.136 --> 00:00:37.536
-Okay.

00:00:37.536 --> 00:00:40.039
-So it stays crunchy on the
outside, soft on the inside.

00:00:40.039 --> 00:00:42.275
It also has a panini maker.
-Alright.

00:00:42.275 --> 00:00:44.543
-Panini in the toaster.
-Oh, that's very exciting.

00:00:44.543 --> 00:00:47.780
We pre-made our paninis
out of the interest of time.

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:51.183
-And, Seth, you can warm up
the cookies if you want to.

00:00:51.183 --> 00:00:52.952
-That's very exciting.
-$510.

00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:54.887
I know it's a little pricey,
guys.

00:00:54.887 --> 00:00:59.125
But $210, 20%, off with
the code "OPRAH." O-P-R-A-H.

00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:00.893
-If you can remember that.
Thanks for spelling it.

00:01:00.893 --> 00:01:02.662
-We think this is cool.
This is cool. Revolution.

00:01:02.662 --> 00:01:04.730
-Now, this is actually --
You are wearing this.

00:01:04.730 --> 00:01:06.599
-Now, this is what
I wanted to change into.

00:01:06.599 --> 00:01:09.902
Because this is a woman who
made this. Small business.

00:01:09.902 --> 00:01:11.737
-Uh-huh.
-Isn't this cute?

00:01:11.737 --> 00:01:13.239
Just backstage, somebody said,
"Gayle, that's very chic."

00:01:13.239 --> 00:01:14.373
-You know,
when you're wearing it,

00:01:14.373 --> 00:01:15.942
you don't have to hold it up
in front of you.

00:01:15.942 --> 00:01:17.577
-Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.577 --> 00:01:19.945
Okay. Okay, Seth.
-Just saying, you know?

00:01:19.945 --> 00:01:23.015
-Okay. This is a size medium.
I'm gonna give it to you.

00:01:23.015 --> 00:01:24.450
-[ Seth speaking muffled ]

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:26.085
-No, I'm gonna give it to you.

00:01:26.085 --> 00:01:28.520
[ Cheers and applause ]
Size medium. Thank you.

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:30.156
I know, but you're right.

00:01:30.156 --> 00:01:33.860
You're right. You're right.
You're right.

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:35.394
You just look like a medium.

00:01:35.394 --> 00:01:36.663
-This is not the "Oprah" show.

00:01:36.663 --> 00:01:38.431
We do not give things
to our guests!

00:01:38.431 --> 00:01:39.999
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.999 --> 00:01:41.835
-That's just from me to you,
ma'am.

00:01:41.835 --> 00:01:42.868
-Alright. That's wonderful.

00:01:42.868 --> 00:01:44.170
-And she looked like
a size medium.

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:45.471
-It looks very comfortable.
-This is a Rivet Utility.

00:01:45.471 --> 00:01:46.739
I think it's chic.

00:01:46.739 --> 00:01:49.108
You can dress it up,
dress it down. $295.

00:01:49.108 --> 00:01:50.376
-Mm-hmm.

00:01:50.376 --> 00:01:52.078
-Oprah lives and breathes
in these, so we like this.

00:01:52.078 --> 00:01:53.646
-I know this is a jigsaw.
-Now, this is puzzle.

00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:55.081
Yeah, we love these.
-Okay. Okay.

00:01:55.081 --> 00:01:56.683
-This happened, you know --
Actually during the pandemic,

00:01:56.683 --> 00:01:58.551
can you imagine Oprah
and Stedman doing puzzles?

00:01:58.551 --> 00:01:59.852
They did.
-They did do puzzles.

00:01:59.852 --> 00:02:01.320
A lot of people I knew
did puzzles.

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:02.689
-Yeah, I saw her
on the Internet.

00:02:02.689 --> 00:02:04.456
I called and said, "Did you guys
really do a puzzle,

00:02:04.456 --> 00:02:05.658
or is that just a shtick?"

00:02:05.658 --> 00:02:07.160
She goes, "No, we really did."

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:08.895
So we like this.
Jiggy Puzzle Kit.

00:02:08.895 --> 00:02:10.530
Something good
for you and your kids.

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:12.598
-Alright. Great.
-Now, this, I think, is great.

00:02:12.598 --> 00:02:15.167
So your kids will --
You've got three children.

00:02:15.167 --> 00:02:16.469
-Uh-huh.
-They like to color.

00:02:16.469 --> 00:02:17.904
They like to draw.

00:02:17.904 --> 00:02:19.505
-See, this makes sense because
I'm not already wearing it.

00:02:19.505 --> 00:02:20.973 line:0%
-Yeah, so, see --

00:02:20.973 --> 00:02:24.310 line:0%
I know. I know, I know.
That was kind of a dweeb move.

00:02:24.310 --> 00:02:26.078
I know, I know, I know.
I know. I get it.

00:02:26.078 --> 00:02:27.713
-So wait. What is --
Tell me about it.

00:02:27.713 --> 00:02:29.582
-Okay, so they draw it,
and then you send it

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:31.550
into this apron company,
and they put it on an apron.

00:02:31.550 --> 00:02:33.519
-Ah, so this is
a child's drawing.

00:02:33.519 --> 00:02:35.955
-So, it comes with all of these.
-Oh, gotcha.

00:02:35.955 --> 00:02:37.423
-So, I think any --

00:02:37.423 --> 00:02:39.459
Anytime you can display
your children's artwork,

00:02:39.459 --> 00:02:40.994
I think that's a good thing.

00:02:40.994 --> 00:02:42.895
This is Cece DuPraz.
Draw your own aprons.

00:02:42.895 --> 00:02:44.964
-Draw your own apron. Beautiful.
-$78.

00:02:44.964 --> 00:02:46.499
We like that, too.

00:02:46.499 --> 00:02:48.868
-Now, can we take a bite of the
cookie that's been warmed here?

00:02:48.868 --> 00:02:50.402
-I want a bite
of the grilled cheese.

00:02:50.402 --> 00:02:52.037
-Yeah, have a bite
of the grilled cheese,

00:02:52.037 --> 00:02:54.473
and then we'll share the cookie.
-Alright.

00:02:54.473 --> 00:02:56.776
-Very warm. It worked.

00:02:56.776 --> 00:02:58.677
-But don't you think
this is cool, though?

00:02:58.677 --> 00:03:00.212
-I think it's very cool.

00:03:00.212 --> 00:03:01.681
-No, you -- Ooh, it is actually
very warm, guys.

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:04.283
-Yeah.
-I don't know why I'm surprised

00:03:04.283 --> 00:03:07.019
because I have
tried this before.

00:03:07.019 --> 00:03:09.555
-That was a crazy thing
for you to say.

00:03:09.555 --> 00:03:10.789
-I know. I know.

00:03:10.789 --> 00:03:14.060
-"It turns out,
I haven't been lying to you."

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:17.697
-I have never lied to you!
Never lied to you!

00:03:17.697 --> 00:03:19.732
-Well, lucky people,
you guys have --

00:03:19.732 --> 00:03:21.634
I guess it's a --
Is it a sweepstakes?

00:03:21.634 --> 00:03:23.402
12 lucky people have a chance
to win all...

00:03:23.402 --> 00:03:26.506
-At OprahDaily.com.
-All 104 items on the list

00:03:26.506 --> 00:03:28.040
on the 12 days
giveaway sweepstakes,

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:29.676
courtesy of Oprah Daily.
-That's right.

00:03:29.676 --> 00:03:31.810
-Visit
OprahDaily.com/favoritethings

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:33.012
for more information.

00:03:33.012 --> 00:03:34.981
You guys,
that's Gayle King, everybody!

00:03:34.981 --> 00:03:36.215
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:36.215 --> 00:03:38.851
The full list
of Oprah's Favorite Things

